In article <1992Nov20.012455.7026@eskimo.com> gregs@eskimo.com (Greg Sumner) writes:


   With all the talk about armor setup, I'd like to get some opinions on
   what's best.  Here's my votes:

   Helm of Telepathy	For seeing monsters before they see you.
Try a Helm of brilliance to increase wiz and int. You can get all the
telepathy you need with a blindfold and the intrinsic.
   GDSM			Obvious reasons
   Gauntlets of Power	Good at the early levels, for carrying and damage.
Prefer Gauntlets of Dexterity
   Boots of Speed		Hey, double attacks.
   Cloak of Displacement	Is it better than invisibility?
Get intrinsic invisibility. The displacement is useful anyway, many
monsters see invisible and displacement can still make them miss.
   Shield of Reflection	This seems to be very very rare.

   Any other input?  If I'm invisible, I dump the cloak of displacement and
   put on an elven cloak.
I'd keep it, as above. For all that, by the time you've amassed that
lot, it's all rather academic, you're probably so powerful etc that
the chances of your being killed in combat is almost zero. A more
interesting question is what one should try to get early on given the
chance (say an unexpected wish or a large armour shop). Under these
circumstances, apart from the above, I reckon the things to look out
for are:-
Cloak of invis: very useful as monsters don't notice you and so don't
chase you around when you'd rather rest. Probably better early on than
cloak of displacement.
Helm of opposite alignment: For those non-chaotics who would like
Stormbringer or non-lawfuls who want Mjollnir.

